  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &#x201c;Challenging Harmful Attitudes and Norms for Gender Equality (CHANGE)&#x201d; is a 36-month EU-funded regional initiative (2026&#x2013;2028) implemented by UNDP, UNFPA, and UN Women across Central Asia, including Uzbekistan. Its overall goal is to contribute to the reduction of gender-based violence (GBV) by addressing its root causes - namely, harmful social norms, gender inequality, and economic vulnerabilities of women.UNDP&#x2019;s work in Uzbekistan under CHANGE combines policy reform, digital innov</narrative>
  </description>
